.TH BT\-DUALBOOT 1 "2026\-09\-12" "bt\-dualboot\-sync 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bt\-dualboot \- sync Bluetooth pairing keys from Linux to Windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bt\-dualboot
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-\-list\-win\-mounts ]
.RB [ \-\-bot ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-win
.IR MOUNT ]
.RB [ \-\-sync
.IR MAC .\|.\|.\&]
.RB [ \-\-sync\-all ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-b
.RI [ path ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Bluetooth device paired under both Linux and Windows stores a different
pairing key in each system, and the device keeps only the most recent one.
On a dualboot machine this means re\-pairing the device after every reboot
into the other system.
.PP
.B bt\-dualboot
copies the pairing keys Linux holds in
.I /var/lib/bluetooth
into the Windows registry hive on a mounted Windows partition, so both systems
authenticate with the same key and the device works in either without being
re\-paired.
.PP
Devices must already be paired in both systems: Windows stores a device only
when it has been paired there, and this tool updates existing entries rather
than creating them.
.PP
The Windows partition must be mounted with write access, and the registry is
edited through
.BR reged (8)
from the chntpw package, which preserves the size of the hive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SS List resources
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-list
List Bluetooth devices, grouped by whether they work in both systems, are
available for sync, still have to be paired in Windows, or have no pairing key
at all. Requires root.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-win\-mounts
List mounted Windows locations that were found.
.TP
.B \-\-bot
Emit parsable output for scripts. Supported together with
.BR \-\-list .
.SS Sync keys
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the actions that would be taken without performing them.
.TP
.BI \-\-win " MOUNT"
Use
.I MOUNT
as the Windows mount point instead of probing for one. Needed only when the
probe finds no Windows installation or finds more than one.
.TP
.BI \-\-sync " MAC" .\|.\|.\&
Sync the devices with the given MAC addresses. Addresses are case insensitive
and separated by spaces. Requires root.
.TP
.B \-\-sync\-all
Sync every paired device that is available for sync. Requires root.
.SS Backup of the Windows registry
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-backup " [path]"
Back up the Windows registry hive before writing to it. Without
.I path
the backup is written to
.IR /var/backup/bt\-dualboot .
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no\-backup
Write to the registry without taking a backup.
.PP
One of
.B \-\-backup
or
.B \-\-no\-backup
has to be given together with
.B \-\-sync
or
.BR \-\-sync\-all ,
so that the choice of backup strategy is always deliberate.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/bluetooth
Linux Bluetooth configuration, holding the pairing keys that are read.
.TP
.I Windows/System32/config/SYSTEM
Registry hive on the mounted Windows partition that is written to.
.TP
.I /var/backup/bt\-dualboot
Default directory for registry backups.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed.
.TP
.B 1
The command line was rejected, a required resource was missing, or the sync
failed. Nothing was changed in the last case.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the devices and their sync status:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo bt\-dualboot \-l
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview what syncing everything would do:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo bt\-dualboot \-\-sync\-all \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sync a single device, backing up the registry first:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo bt\-dualboot \-\-sync C2:9E:1D:E2:3D:A5 \-\-backup
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reged (8),
.BR chntpw (8),
.BR bluetoothctl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/vhrabar/bt\-dualboot/issues
.UE .
